      "message": "If I read cppreference correctly this leads to copy-list-initialization. This means parsed_reacord will be copied (not moved) into the returned pair. Since the constructed pair is a prvalue, copy-elision will then kick in. But the whole record would have been copied.\nYou should use\nreturn { error, std::move(parsed_record)};\nto avoid this copy.\n\n[1] https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return (see variant 2)\n[2] https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/list_initialization",
